abstract: >
  Python implementation of a Lagrangian particle-tracking CFD model for
  predicting ascorbic acid (vitamin C) retention during spray drying of
  Myrciaria dubia (camu camu) extract. Includes Box-Behnken Response Surface
  Methodology, Monte Carlo uncertainty quantification, Morris global
  sensitivity analysis, and glass transition temperature analysis.

keywords:
  - spray drying
  - camu camu
  - Myrciaria dubia
  - ascorbic acid
  - CFD
  - Lagrangian simulation
  - response surface methodology
  - Box-Behnken design
  - Monte Carlo
  - food engineering

